      "tag": "p",
      "text": "FAQ"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "How often should I review my financial data?"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "We recommend reviewing your financial data at least once a week. Regular check-ins help you stay on top of your spending, track progress toward your goals, and make informed decisions."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "What kind of financial data can I track with this app?"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "You can track a wide range of financial data, including income, expenses, budgets, savings, debt, and even investments. The app gives you a full picture of your financial health in one place."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Can I track my spending automatically?"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Yes! You can connect your bank accounts and credit cards to the app to automatically import and categorize your transactions, making spending tracking effortless."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Does the app offer investment tracking?"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Absolutely. You can link your investment accounts to monitor portfolio performance, asset allocation, and more — all in real time."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "How do I sign up for the app?"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Signing up is simple. Just download the app from the App Store or Google Play, follow the on-screen setup steps, and you’ll be up and running in minutes."
